{"additions":4074,"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTA5NDkz","is_bot":false,"login":"td72","name":"Kohei Hosokawa"},"body":"## Summary\n\nA read-only **Projects view** (slot 7, key `7`) for GitHub Projects (v2): the repository owner's projects on the left, the selected project as a kanban board (or a sortable table) on the right, and an item detail below. Data comes from `gh project list / field-list / item-list --format json`, `gh repo view` and one GraphQL read (`updatedAt`); issue / PR bodies use `gh issue view` / `gh pr view --repo`. Nothing adds, moves, edits or deletes anything.\n\n![projects demo](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/td72/vig/feat/projects-view/assets/demo-projects.gif)\n\n## Changes\n\n- **Page skeleton** (`src/projects/`): `page.rs`, `state.rs` (`ProjectsBgMessage` over `mpsc`, drained in `drain_background()`, lazy init on first `on_activate`, list re-fetched when the page is re-activated after 5 min), `domain/{client,types,disk_cache}.rs`, `panes/{projects,board,detail}.rs`; `build_pages` arm, `page \"projects\"` KDL block, `\"7\" \"page:projects\"`, `projects` appended to `pages`, `Config::projects_page()`, header / status bar.\n- **Availability**: missing `gh` → \"gh not available\" notice; a `gh project` error mentioning the `project` / `read:project` scope → `gh needs the project scope: run \\`gh auth refresh -s project\\``; other errors go to the status bar.\n- **Project list pane** (22 %): `#n title` + `n items · 3d ago`; projects linked to the current repository (`gh repo view --json projectsV2`) come first, marked `▸`; `/` search; selection loads the board (memory → disk cache → fetch); `r` re-fetches.\n- **Board pane**: columns = `Status` single-select options in GitHub's order, then any status the field no longer lists, then `No status` when some item has none. Cards: `●` issue / `⇅` PR / `✎` draft, `#number`, title, `@assignees` + labels. `h` / `l` / `←` / `→` move between columns, `j` / `k` within, columns narrower than 24 cells scroll horizontally (`Board #2 (columns 1-3 of 5)`), `/` searches titles and numbers across columns. `t` toggles **table mode**: `#`, Title, Assignees, then the project's own fields (Status, Priority, Estimate, Iteration, dates, custom text / number — GitHub-managed fields like Labels / Repository are left to the detail); `s` (or `h` / `l`) cycles the sort column — numeric when every cell is a number, option order for Status, case-insensitive text otherwise, empty cells last. `Enter` / `i` focus the detail, `o` opens the item (drafts open the project), `Esc` goes back to the list. `--limit 500` truncation shows `(truncated at 500)` in the status bar.\n- **Detail pane**: header (issue / PR: the GitHub page's author / date / state / labels badges; otherwise kind + repository), a `Fields` section with every field value of the item (Status first, then field-list order), then the markdown body and comments via the GitHub page's `markdown_to_lines` (drafts: their body). Fetches are cached per `owner/repo#n`; `h` / `←` / `Esc` return to the board.\n- GitHub client: `get_issue_in` / `get_pr_in` (`--repo`) so items from other repositories resolve; `markdown_to_lines`, `build_issue_header`, `build_pr_header`, `format_date` are now `pub(crate)`.\n- Docs: README / README.ja (Features, `7` row, Projects View section), `docs/config.md`, CLAUDE.md. Demo: `tape/demo-projects.tape` + `assets/demo-projects.gif`, `mise run demo:projects` (in `demo:all`).\n- Tests: JSON fixtures (project list, repo info, field list, item list with issue / PR / draft / redacted items), column grouping, table columns and sorting, `value_text` shapes, scope / missing-CLI detection, disk-cache roundtrip, pane navigation (columns, table toggle keeps the selection, search, refresh keeps the item), detail loading / stale results, state flow (list → board → detail, notices), KDL wiring, `pages` / `page_keys` now `1..7`.\n\n## Not verified\n\n- Organization-owned projects and iteration / date / number custom fields were only exercised through fixtures (the demo board has none); the `gh` key naming (`camelCase` of the field name) was checked against the `gh` source.\n- The scope-missing notice was tested with the recorded `gh` error text, not against a token that actually lacks the scope.\n- Boards with more than 500 items (the truncation flag) and more columns than fit the pane (horizontal scrolling) were unit-tested, not recorded.\n\nCloses #119, closes #120, closes #121, closes #122, closes #123\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01TreGn5Xh4PjDRv9Yo4QU4w\n","changedFiles":26,"comments":[],"createdAt":"2026-08-30T09:28:23Z","deletions":41,"headRefName":"feat/projects-view","labels":[],"number":125,"reviewDecision":"","reviews":[{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLaBNfQ","author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"### 🟡 Changes recommended\n\nThere are verified performance/behavior issues in the new Projects implementation (unconditional disk-cache read when disabled, and avoidable per-compare allocations in sorting) that should be addressed before approval.\n\n*Once you've addressed the issues Copilot identified, you can request another Copilot review.*\n\n<details>\n<summary>Pull request overview</summary>\n\nAdds a new read-only **Projects** page to vig that browses GitHub Projects (v2) via the `gh` CLI, integrating it into the existing multi-page TUI (config wiring, page switching, UI chrome, and demos/docs).\n\n**Changes:**\n- Introduces `src/projects/` (page state, panes, domain client/types, disk cache) implementing project list → board/table → item detail flow.\n- Wires the new page into app/page infrastructure (page registry, config loader, status bar/header, default KDL, page switching keys/tests).\n- Updates documentation and demo assets (README/JA README/config docs, VHS tape + LFS GIF, mise tasks).\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>File summaries</summary>\n\n| File | Description |\r\n| ---- | ----------- |\r\n| tape/demo-projects.tape | Adds VHS recording script for Projects demo GIF. |\r\n| src/projects/state.rs | Implements Projects page state, background fetching, and notices. |\r\n| src/projects/panes/projects.rs | Project list pane (selection, search, open/focus actions). |\r\n| src/projects/panes/board.rs | Board/table pane rendering, navigation, sorting, search, open actions. |\r\n| src/projects/panes/detail.rs | Detail pane rendering and background fetch for issue/PR details. |\r\n| src/projects/panes/mod.rs | Exposes Projects panes modules. |\r\n| src/projects/page.rs | Registers Projects `new_page()` constructor. |\r\n| src/projects/mod.rs | Adds Projects module structure. |\r\n| src/projects/domain/client.rs | Wraps `gh project`/GraphQL reads for projects/boards. |\r\n| src/projects/domain/types.rs | Defines JSON shapes + board/table grouping and sorting logic. |\r\n| src/projects/domain/disk_cache.rs | Adds disk cache for project list and boards. |\r\n| src/projects/domain/mod.rs | Exposes Projects domain modules. |\r\n| src/pages.rs | Registers `projects` in `build_pages`. |\r\n| src/main.rs | Adds `mod projects;` to compile the new page. |\r\n| src/core/ui/status_bar.rs | Adds Projects header and status bar rendering. |\r\n| src/core/config/loader.rs | Adds `projects_page()` accessor + builtin config tests updates. |\r\n| src/core/app.rs | Updates builtin pages/keys/help to include slot 7 = Projects. |\r\n| src/github/domain/client.rs | Adds `get_issue_in` / `get_pr_in` for cross-repo items. |\r\n| src/github/panes/detail_view/view.rs | Exposes markdown/header/date helpers for reuse by Projects detail. |\r\n| assets/default.kdl | Adds `page \"projects\"` block and binds key `7` to it. |\r\n| README.md | Documents Projects view and adds keybinding row. |\r\n| docs/README.ja.md | Japanese docs for Projects view and keybindings. |\r\n| docs/config.md | Documents `projects` page name and its panes/actions. |\r\n| mise.toml | Adds `demo:projects` task and includes it in `demo:all`. |\r\n| assets/demo-projects.gif | Adds Projects demo GIF via Git LFS pointer. |\r\n| CLAUDE.md | Updates architecture overview to include Projects page. |\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review details</summary>\n\n- **Files reviewed:** 26/26 changed files\n- **Comments generated:** 3\n- **Review effort level:** Lite\n</details>\n\n---\n\n💡 <a href=\"/td72/vig/new/main?filename=.github/skills/code-review/SKILL.md\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Add a `code-review` agent skill</a> or configure MCP servers for context-aware, tailored reviews. <a href=\"https://docs.github.com/copilot/how-tos/use-copilot-agents/request-a-code-review/use-code-review?tool=webui#mcp-servers-and-agent-skills\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Learn more in the docs.</a>","submittedAt":"2026-08-30T09:32:13Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"360cbba1d80950b4c0f1bc94c98f1b6e8256c0f9"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLaExbw","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-08-30T10:06:36Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"eb44f4de43544208e05b73b34f64a3bb024c58da"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLaExqg","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-08-30T10:06:38Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"eb44f4de43544208e05b73b34f64a3bb024c58da"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLaEx3g","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-08-30T10:06:40Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"eb44f4de43544208e05b73b34f64a3bb024c58da"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLaFIEQ","author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"### 🔵 Needs a closer look\n\nThe Projects repo-info deserialization appears to use an incorrect `projectsV2` connection key (`Nodes`) and the linked-project ordering helper uses an unstable sort despite claiming stable ordering, which can break linked-project detection and produce nondeterministic UI ordering.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review details</summary>\n\n### Suppressed comments (3)\n\n**Previously missed (2)** — in code that hasn't changed since the last review.\n\n**src/projects/domain/types.rs:37**\n* `gh repo view --json owner,projectsV2` is expected to return a lower-camel-case `nodes` array for the connection; deserializing from `\"Nodes\"` will likely prevent linked project detection and reorder/marker logic from working.\n\nThis issue also appears on line 631 of the same file.\n```\n#[derive(Debug, Clone, Default, Deserialize)]\npub struct LinkedProjects {\n    #[serde(rename = \"Nodes\", default)]\n    pub nodes: Vec<LinkedProject>,\n```\n**src/projects/domain/types.rs:109**\n* `order_projects` claims to keep the relative order of linked projects, but `sort_by_key` is an unstable sort and may reorder projects that compare equal (both linked or both unlinked). This can make the UI ordering nondeterministic across runs.\n```\npub fn order_projects(mut projects: Vec<Project>, linked: &[u64]) -> Vec<Project> {\n    for p in &mut projects {\n        p.linked = linked.contains(&p.number);\n    }\n    projects.sort_by_key(|p| !p.linked);\n```\n\n**src/projects/domain/types.rs:635**\n* This unit test JSON uses `projectsV2.Nodes`, but the deserializer should match the actual `gh repo view` output key (`nodes`). As written, the test will lock in the wrong shape and mask a real parsing failure.\n```\n    #[test]\n    fn parses_repo_info_with_and_without_linked_projects() {\n        let json = r#\"{\"name\":\"vig\",\"owner\":{\"id\":\"X\",\"login\":\"td72\"},\"projectsV2\":{\"Nodes\":[{\"id\":\"PVT_1\",\"title\":\"vig demo board\",\"number\":2,\"closed\":false}]}}\"#;\n        let info: RepoInfo = serde_json::from_str(json).unwrap();\n        assert_eq!(info.owner.login, \"td72\");\n```\n\n- **Files reviewed:** 26/26 changed files\n- **Comments generated:** 0 new\n- **Review effort level:** Lite\n</details>","submittedAt":"2026-08-30T10:10:04Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"eb44f4de43544208e05b73b34f64a3bb024c58da"}}],"state":"MERGED","statusCheckRollup":[{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-30T10:12:38Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33305917215/job/99242358278","name":"create-tag","startedAt":"2026-08-30T10:12:47Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Release"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-30T10:07:48Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33305656433/job/99241637918","name":"build (x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu, ubuntu-latest)","startedAt":"2026-08-30T10:06:23Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-30T10:07:04Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33305656445/job/99241637873","name":"lint","startedAt":"2026-08-30T10:06:24Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CI"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-30T10:07:35Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33305656433/job/99241637861","name":"build (aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu, ubuntu-24.04-arm)","startedAt":"2026-08-30T10:06:25Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-30T10:07:58Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33305656433/job/99241637939","name":"build (aarch64-apple-darwin, macos-latest)","startedAt":"2026-08-30T10:06:24Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-30T10:07:58Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33305656433/job/99241838530","name":"upload","startedAt":"2026-08-30T10:07:59Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-30T10:12:38Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33305917215/job/99242345364","name":"publish","startedAt":"2026-08-30T10:12:39Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Release"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-30T10:07:21Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33305656445/job/99241637948","name":"test (x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu, ubuntu-latest)","startedAt":"2026-08-30T10:06:23Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CI"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-30T10:07:42Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33305656445/job/99241637941","name":"test (aarch64-apple-darwin, macos-latest)","startedAt":"2026-08-30T10:06:24Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CI"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-30T10:12:38Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33305917215/job/99242361848","name":"homebrew","startedAt":"2026-08-30T10:12:49Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Release"}],"title":"✨ Projects view: GitHub Projects boards"}
